# Cloudflare Pages routing for the dual-entry PWA.
#
# The landing page is the front door at `/` (lightweight, no PixiJS/Three/Dexie).
# The interactive app lives at `/app` and its sub-paths.
#
# Why /app is a real directory (dist/app/index.html) instead of a _redirects
# rewrite to /index.html:
#   Cloudflare's pretty-URL normalization runs BEFORE _redirects rules and emits
#   hard 308s for any request whose path matches an asset after normalization
#   (e.g. /app -> / for dist/index.html, /index.html -> /). Those 308s cannot be
#   shadowed by rewrite (200) rules, so /app must not normalize onto an asset
#   path. Serving /app/ from a real directory index avoids normalization
#   entirely. See docs/infra/cloudflare-pages-routing.md.

# Landing page is the root entry.
/          /landing.html   200

# App shell: /app normalizes to /app/ (308), which serves dist/app/index.html.
# Sub-paths and unknown paths fall back to the app shell for client-side routes.
/app/*     /app/index.html     200
